ts=2026-04-17T02:00:55.718Z type=context scope=codebase:tempest-tradingview-mcp content="As of 2026-04-17, src/tempest_mcp/indicators/structure.py is a small legacy flat module with calculate_fibonacci_levels(...) and calculate_pivot_points(...). No internal Python imports of those helpers were found, and Fibonacci is not exported from indicators/__init__.py or registered in tools/server." issue=ENG-29 tags=indicators,fibonacci,structure.py,backlog-review
ts=2026-04-17T04:20:16.656Z type=pattern scope=shion:reviews content="When refactoring legacy helpers into new engines, watch for 'compatibility wrappers' that silently change semantics (e.g., ignored parameters like trend='down'). Tests sometimes get updated to the new behavior, masking backward-compat regressions; explicitly diff old vs new behavior and pin tests to legacy semantics unless intentionally breaking." issue=ENG-29 Fibonacci engine tags=qa,regression,compatibility,tests
ts=2026-04-17T04:24:29.012Z type=learning scope=raphael:tempest-tradingview-mcp content="For ENG-29 Fibonacci validation, Shion's numeric-type concern was valid overall but np.float64 specifically did not fail in this Python/numpy environment; np.int64 still failed with isinstance(..., int). Using numbers.Real is the right compatibility fix for swing/level/tolerance validators." issue=ENG-29 tags=python,numpy,validation,eng-29
ts=2026-04-17T04:26:47.677Z type=learning scope=shion:linear content="In this workspace, Linear GraphQL `issue(id: \"ENG-29\")` accepts the human identifier (team key + number) directly; IssueFilter does not support `identifier` field. Use `issue(id:\"ENG-xx\")` or `issueSearch` to fetch issue + comments reliably." issue=ENG-29 lane B rerun context fetch tags=linear,graphql,workflow
ts=2026-04-17T07:23:31.727Z type=context scope=codebase:tempest-tradingview-mcp content="As of 2026-04-17 backlog review ENG-30: there is no TPO implementation in the repo. The architecture-fit surface is a new pure indicator module at src/tempest_mcp/indicators/volume/tpo.py with direct tests under tests/test_indicators/. Existing tool/server surfaces for later analytical exposure already live in src/tempest_mcp/tools/analysis_tools.py and src/tempest_mcp/server.py, so TPO MCP wiring should remain a separate ticket. Main backlog ambiguity is session ownership/marker contract for Initial Balance and range expansion." issue=ENG-30 tags=backlog-review,tpo,indicators,analysis-tools,architecture-fit
ts=2026-04-17T07:26:36.858Z type=pattern scope=codebase:tempest-tradingview-mcp content="Indicator-layer feature tickets in tempest-tradingview-mcp should align to the src-based package layout under src/tempest_mcp/indicators, typically return deterministic pandas DataFrames plus attrs metadata (e.g. volume_profile), and should add boundary tests preventing drift into tools/server when scope is engine-only." issue=ENG-30 tags=python,indicators,backlog-review,architecture,tests
ts=2026-04-17T07:26:36.886Z type=pattern scope=raphael:structural-reviews content="For Tempest ENG backlog reviews, verify Linear type labels against exact workflow casing (`feature`, `bug`, `refactor`, etc.); mismatched capitalization like `Feature` is a structural correction worth calling out." issue=ENG-30 tags=linear,workflow,backlog-review
ts=2026-04-17T14:52:28.358Z type=decision scope=shuna:eng-30 content="ENG-30 design scope is indicator-only: implement calculate_tpo_chart in src/tempest_mcp/indicators/volume/tpo.py with deterministic DataFrame schema and attrs metadata; no tools/server work until ENG-37." issue=ENG-30 tags=design,tpo,indicator-layer,scope-boundary
ts=2026-04-17T14:52:28.364Z type=pattern scope=codebase:tempest-tradingview-mcp content="For market-profile engines, keep pure pandas math in indicators/volume with strict OHLCV validation, deterministic output ordering, top-level exports via indicators.volume and indicators.__all__, and boundary tests that forbid imports from tools/server modules." issue=ENG-30 tags=architecture,indicator-pattern,boundary-test,exports
ts=2026-04-17T18:13:57.763Z type=context scope=codebase:tempest-tradingview-mcp content="Repo contract for indicator work: pure analytical engines live under src/tempest_mcp/indicators/, MCP exposure belongs in src/tempest_mcp/tools/ and server.py, and deterministic indicator tests live under tests/test_indicators/. Existing Elliott strategy/tool surface still uses legacy 'elliot_wave' spelling while new analytical work may use corrected 'elliott' naming, so design reviews should resolve naming explicitly." issue=ENG-31 tags=architecture,indicators,naming,linear-review
ts=2026-04-17T18:50:28.435Z type=decision scope=shuna:eng-31 content="For ENG-31, the new indicator-layer analytical API is standardized on corrected `elliott` naming (double t), while all legacy Phase 2 strategy/tool identifiers remain frozen as `elliot_wave` (single t) for compatibility. ENG-31 remains indicators-only with no server/tool/backtest wiring changes." issue=ENG-31 tags=architecture,naming-boundary,indicator-layer,linear
ts=2026-04-17T18:50:28.465Z type=context scope=codebase:tempest-tradingview-mcp content="Repo contract reaffirmed for ENG-31: indicator analytics belong in src/tempest_mcp/indicators (structure.py public surface), MCP exposure remains in src/tempest_mcp/tools + server.py (ENG-37), and deterministic indicator tests live in tests/test_indicators. Legacy Phase 2 IDs retain `elliot_wave` spelling." issue=ENG-31 tags=repo-contract,indicators,mcp-boundary,compatibility
ts=2026-04-17T19:24:34.241Z type=pattern scope=shion:python-validation content="When validating numeric pandas Series, `np.isfinite(series).all()` can raise TypeError if dtype is object/non-numeric; prefer `pd.to_numeric(..., errors='coerce')` + `np.isfinite` or catch TypeError and raise ValueError for consistent failure mode (DoS-hardening)." issue=ENG-31 tags=python,pandas,input-validation,dos
ts=2026-04-17T19:39:57.475Z type=pattern scope=codebase:tempest-tradingview-mcp content="For Elliott wave detection, swing extraction should confirm alternating pivot legs and apply min_swing_pct to move size between confirmed pivots rather than to the local-window extremum itself; sequence-level acceptance should be assigned uniformly across all rows in a candidate sequence." issue=ENG-31 tags=elliott-wave,indicators,swing-detection,acceptance-metadata
ts=2026-04-17T19:43:41.570Z type=pattern scope=shion:lane-b content="During Lane B re-reviews, always check whether reported fixes are committed/pushed (git status + branch vs origin). If fixes exist only as local dirty changes, treat as FAIL until landed, even if tests pass locally." issue=ENG-31 Lane B re-review found fixes uncommitted tags=qa,lane-b,git,process,merge-readiness
